  "brief": "This flow arms at astronomical dusk (\u221230 min). It then arms M16. M16 is a 3x2 mosaic of 6 panels at 25% overlap, laid out at PA 30\u00b0 with the rotator turned to it at every panel. After 1 pass of its filters on a panel it moves on to the next (least complete first), and comes back until every panel has its subs. A hop between panels takes about 2 m 40 s, as measured on this rig. For M16 it captures Ha 300 s \u00d7 2 (gain 100, bin 1). It then arms M31. For M31 it captures L 60 s \u00d7 5 (gain 100, bin 1). It then selects the best of M13, M92 - above 30\u00b0, at least 40\u00b0 from the moon (if up), within 4 h of the meridian. For every member of the pool it captures L 60 s \u00d7 5 (gain 100, bin 1). If the active target sinks to the 30\u00b0 floor, it is set aside for tonight - a restart tonight does not retry it, the next night does - and the next best takes over.",
